course: dictionary
lesson: 1369
title: Same word, different meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word canton can mean a region of a country, a corner of a flag, or an old name for a city. The sentence around it tells you which meaning is right. «Switzerland has no official capital by law, and Bern is called the federal city... the country is made of 26 cantons (regions)...» The words «made of» and «regions» are the clues: canton means region here.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Switzerland is made of 26 regions fits perfectly, so the region meaning is correct. Then test your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well.
explain: A flag or a city can also be called a canton, so you must check the other words. If the sentence talks about flags, stars and poles, it means the corner of the flag. If it talks about Guangzhou or Cantonese, it means the old English name for that city.
fact: «Canton» means one of the regions that Switzerland is divided into. Switzerland has 26 cantons.
fact: Each Swiss canton has its own government, and Zurich, Geneva and Bern are all cantons.
fact: On a flag, the canton is the top corner next to the pole. The US flag has its stars in the canton.
fact: «Canton» is also the old English name for Guangzhou, a big city in southern China.
fact: Cantonese is the language and food that come from Guangzhou, and it is spoken in Hong Kong too.
exercise: «Switzerland is made of 26 cantons (regions).» What does canton mean here? | *A region of a country | A pole for holding a flag | A large bird that cannot fly | A type of cheese
exercise: The US flag has its stars in the canton. Where is the canton on a flag? | *The top corner next to the pole | Along the stripes | The very middle | The bottom edge
exercise: Cantonese food and language come from Guangzhou. What is Cantonese? | A kind of flag | A mountain | *A language | A type of boat
test: Which of these is a canton of Switzerland? | Guangzhou | Madrid | *Geneva | Paris
test: Which is the old English name for Guangzhou? | Cantor | *Canton | Cantata | Canteen
exam: Why can the same word canton mean different things in geography and flag lessons? | Because maps and flags are the same thing | Because it is a spelling mistake | Because flags are always made in Switzerland | *Because one word can have several meanings, and the sentence shows which one fits
